  "description": "EfficientNet-B0 pretrained backbone with 1\u21923 channel expansion, SpecAugment (freq_mask=24, time_mask=48, 2 masks each), focal loss (gamma=2, alpha=0.75) for long-tail classes, mixup (alpha=0.4), dropout 0.4 before the 206-unit sigmoid head, cosine-annealing LR schedule (init_lr=1e-3, T_max=30, eta_min=1e-6), AdamW (wd=1e-4), trained for 30 epochs with input size 224\u00d7224.",
  "reasoning": "The best result so far (0.4757) used efficientnet_b0 with mixup and heavy dropout. To push further, I add focal loss to directly address the long-tail minority-class problem which is the stated hard case, SpecAugment for stronger audio-domain regularization, and cosine annealing for smoother convergence. These are complementary improvements targeting the specific weaknesses (rare class recall, overfitting) without changing the proven backbone."
}

